s that the bond between humans and dogs triggers the same neurological responses as the bond between parents and children. Oxytocin—the 'love hormone'—floods our brains when we're with our dogs, creating a connection that is biologically as real as any human relationship.<\/p>\n  <\/div>\n<\/div>","column_1_image_first":"image_first","column_1_img_pt":0,"column_1_img_prl":0,"column_1_img_pb":0,"show_column_2":false,"column_2_align_desktop":"top","column_2_html":"<h2>Column 2<\/h2>\n<p>Add HTML here.<\/p>","column_2_image_first":"image_first","column_2_img_pt":0,"column_2_img_prl":0,"column_2_img_pb":0,"show_column_3":false,"column_3_align_desktop":"top","column_3_html":"<h2>Column 3<\/h2>\n<p>Add HTML here.<\/p>","column_3_image_first":"image_first","column_3_img_pt":0,"column_3_img_prl":0,"column_3_img_pb":0}},"custom_section_4MP8XD":{"type":"custom-section","custom_css":[".info-box-container {display: flex; gap: 24px; max-width: 832px; margin: auto;}",".info-box-icon-container {background: #f2f0ef; width: 56px; height: 56px; display: flex; justify-content: center; align-items: center; border-radius: 16px;}",".info-box-icon-container svg {color: var(--dgg-blue);}",".info-box-header {font-size: 24px; margin-bottom: 16px; font-weight: 500;}",".info-box-body {font-size: 16px; font-weight: 500;}","@media screen and (max-width: 480px) {.info-box-container {flex-direction: column; }}"],"name":"Custom Section","settings":{"content_key":"","bg_type":"solid","background_color":"#fdf8f3","center_content":false,"background_gradient":"linear-gradient(135deg, #9FAECC 0%, #E8C547 100%)","gap_desktop":24,"gap_mobile":16,"pt_desktop":0,"prl_desktop":24,"pb_desktop":48,"pt_mobile":0,"prl_mobile":16,"pb_mobile":48,"additional_css":"","column_1_align_desktop":"top","column_1_html":"<div class=\"info-box-container\">\n  <div>\n    <div class=\"info-box-icon-container\">\n      <svg xmlns=\"http:\/\/www.w3.org\/2000\/svg\" width=\"28\" height=\"28\" viewbox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-heart text-[#9BA8C4]\"><path d=\"M19 14c1.49-1.46 3-3.21 3-5.5A5.5 5.5 0 0 0 16.5 3c-1.76 0-3 .5-4.5 2-1.5-1.5-2.74-2-4.5-2A5.5 5.5 0 0 0 2 8.5c0 2.3 1.5 4.05 3 5.5l7 7Z\"><\/path><\/svg>\n    <\/div>\n  <\/div>\n  <div>\n    <h2 class=\"info-box-header\">Why It Hurts So Much<\/h2>\n    <p class=\"info-box-body\">Studies have found that grieving a pet can be as intense as grieving a human family member. This isn't weakness or exaggeration—it's biology. Your brain formed real attachment bonds, and breaking those bonds causes real pain.<\/p>\n  <\/div>\n<\/div>","column_1_image_first":"image_first","column_1_img_pt":0,"column_1_img_prl":0,"column_1_img_pb":0,"show_column_2":false,"column_2_align_desktop":"top","column_2_html":"<h2>Column 2<\/h2>\n<p>Add HTML here.<\/p>","column_2_image_first":"image_first","column_2_img_pt":0,"column_2_img_prl":0,"column_2_img_pb":0,"show_column_3":false,"column_3_align_desktop":"top","column_3_html":"<h2>Column 3<\/h2>\n<p>Add HTML here.<\/p>","column_3_image_first":"image_first","column_3_img_pt":0,"column_3_img_prl":0,"column_3_img_pb":0}},"custom_section_PRLaqX":{"type":"custom-section","custom_css":[".info-box-container {display: flex; gap: 24px; max-width: 832px; margin: auto;}",".info-box-icon-container {background: #f2f0ef; width: 56px; height: 56px; display: flex; justify-content: center; align-items: center; border-radius: 16px;}",".info-box-icon-container svg {color: var(--dgg-blue);}",".info-box-header {font-size: 24px; margin-bottom: 16px; font-weight: 500;}",".info-box-body {font-size: 16px; font-weight: 500;}","@media screen and (max-width: 480px) {.info-box-container {flex-direction: column; }}"],"name":"Custom Section","settings":{"content_key":"","bg_type":"solid","background_color":"#fdf8f3","center_content":false,"background_gradient":"linear-gradient(135deg, #9FAECC 0%, #E8C547 100%)","gap_desktop":24,"gap_mobile":16,"pt_desktop":0,"prl_desktop":24,"pb_desktop":48,"pt_mobile":0,"prl_mobile":16,"pb_mobile":48,"additional_css":"","column_1_align_desktop":"top","column_1_html":"<div class=\"info-box-container\">\n  <div>\n    <div class=\"info-box-icon-container\">\n      <svg xmlns=\"http:\/\/www.w3.org\/2000\/svg\" width=\"28\" height=\"28\" viewbox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-users text-[#9BA8C4]\"><path d=\"M16 21v-2a4 4 0 0 0-4-4H6a4 4 0 0 0-4 4v2\"><\/path><circle cx=\"9\" cy=\"7\" r=\"4\"><\/circle><path d=\"M22 21v-2a4 4 0 0 0-3-3.87\"><\/path><path d=\"M16 3.13a4 4 0 0 1 0 7.75\"><\/path><\/svg>\n    <\/div>\n  <\/div>\n  <div>\n    <h2 class=\"info-box-header\">Disenfranchised Grief<\/h2>\n    <p class=\"info-box-body\">Psychologists call pet loss 'disenfranchised grief'—a type of mourning that society often doesn't fully acknowledge. This can make the experience even harder, as grievers may feel they need to hide or minimize their pain.<\/p>\n  <\/div>\n<\/div>","column_1_image_first":"image_first","column_1_img_pt":0,"column_1_img_prl":0,"column_1_img_pb":0,"show_column_2":false,"column_2_align_desktop":"top","column_2_html":"<h2>Column 2<\/h2>\n<p>Add HTML here.<\/p>","column_2_image_first":"image_first","column_2_img_pt":0,"column_2_img_prl":0,"column_2_img_pb":0,"show_column_3":false,"column_3_align_desktop":"top","column_3_html":"<h2>Column 3<\/h2>\n<p>Add HTML here.<\/p>","column_3_image_first":"image_first","column_3_img_pt":0,"column_3_img_prl":0,"column_3_img_pb":0}},"custom_section_VmFMxK":{"type":"custom-section","custom_css":[".info-box-container {display: flex; gap: 24px; max-width: 832px; margin: auto;}",".info-box-icon-container {background: #f2f0ef; width: 56px; height: 56px; display: flex; justify-content: center; align-items: center; border-radius: 16px;}",".info-box-icon-container svg {color: var(--dgg-blue);}",".info-bo